mdmota@yahoo.com.au wrote:
[Hearse on multiple NH installs]
> Can this be worked around by (in my case) editing the original slashem
> bones files (but not changing them) so that the date last modified is
> after the nethack bones upload?

You *could* run touch or some similar utility on them.

An easier workaround:

1. Set system clock to something relatively ancient, e.g. 1/1/2000
2. Run "hearse /r" - this will reset the last-uploaded-date to now and 
exit immediately without doing any work
3. Set system clock back to today's date
4. Run Hearse again from your Slashem directory to upload your bones 
files

That'll only have to be done once so you can upload your backlog of 
Slashem files.  The only other thing you need to do is to remember to 
run Hearse after playing a game in any of your NH installs that creates 
a bones file (or, more simply, just run Hearse after every NH game).  
That'll make sure the different games don't get out of sync.

This is obviously far from ideal, and I will be addressing this when I 
have some free time over the summer.  An overhaul of some of the minor 
niggles in the client is long overdue.

